        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-29T18:20:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we are here or in the other hw_ variant and the tilemodes are not clamp, the subset needs to be adjusted to [-really-big, +really-big] since the shader is universally applying the clamp.\n\nAlternatively, we could use the sign of `fLinearFilterUVInset` to specify whether or not the subset should be applied. \n\nSince the UV inset parameter is 2 components and should always be positive if we are going to use it for real values, we could also use that to eliminate the extra `filterMode` uniform. Sign-encode the X channel as negative if we are doing the UV coord snapping to centers, and sign-encode the Y channel as negative if we are doign the clamp calls.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 778,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 778,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "ef827b67ee2d35b5b773bab7bc34816815c8d97e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
